# A spring: x'' = -x, written as two first-order equations, Dx = v, Dv = -x,
# from x = 1, v = 0. The answer is x = cos t, v = -sin t. With h = 0.1 the
# values at the end are within a few units in the sixth digit of
# cos 3 = -.98999250 and -sin 3 = -.14112001. t itself is typed .29999992+01:
# a tenth is not exact in binary, and t has had it added thirty times.
    t = 0,
    h = 0.1,
    x = 1,
    v = 0,
1   PRINT t, x, v.
    n = 0,
2   Dx = v,
    Dv = -x,
    n = n + 1,
    e = n - 4.5,
    CP 2,
    e = t - 2.95,
    CP 1,
    PRINT t, x, v.
    STOP
